Upstream / third-party
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

VuruşKoç began as a fork of and still contains code from:

  SwingForge AI — https://github.com/SinbadSails/SwingForge
    MIT License. The tennis-swing scoring/coaching core (core/*.py) and the
    Gradio UI originate here and remain available under MIT from that project.

  tennis_analysis — https://github.com/abdullahtarek/tennis_analysis
    SwingForge is in turn built on this project (YOLO player/ball detection,
    court keypoint detection, video pipeline). Those modules (trackers/,
    court_line_detector/, mini_court/, pipeline.py, yolo_inference.py) are
    legacy and unused by the shipped on-device app.

Bundled models / data:
  * MediaPipe Pose Landmarker (pose_landmarker_lite.task) — Google, Apache-2.0.
  * data/pros/*.json — pose keypoints extracted with MediaPipe from publicly
    available slow-motion coaching / practice footage, used for reference only.

Runtime dependencies keep their own licenses (React — MIT, @mediapipe/tasks-vision
— Apache-2.0, Inter & Space Grotesk fonts — SIL OFL 1.1, etc.).

The combined work is distributed under the AGPL-3.0-or-later. Files that carry an
upstream MIT copyright keep that notice; the license of the whole does not
diminish the rights you have to the upstream projects from their own repos.
